# ENC-TSK-G43: cross-Lambda module sharing manifest. Each non-comment line is a
# repo-relative path to a single file; _build.yml copies it to the function root
# so the Lambda can `import` it normally.
#
# DVP-TSK-665: same reasoning as backend/lambda/governance_mart/.build_extras.
# health_surface.py tries `from enceladus_shared.warehouse_registration import ...`
# first and falls back to `from warehouse_registration import ...`. The first
# path cannot resolve on the deployed function: SharedLayerArn is pinned to
# enceladus-shared:10, defined as ":7 + appconfig_flags", and
# warehouse_registration landed later (DVP-TSK-668/669/670). Vendoring it here is
# what makes the fallback branch resolve. When a shared-layer version containing
# warehouse_registration is published AND the canonical pin is bumped, the layer
# wins the try branch and this line can go.
#
# Flattened to the function root by _build.yml, so the import name is
# `warehouse_registration` — NOT `enceladus_shared.warehouse_registration`.
backend/lambda/shared_layer/python/enceladus_shared/warehouse_registration.py
